          },
          "description": "Stores frequently asked questions.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "faqId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the FAQ."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/appointmentSlots/{appointmentSlotId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "AppointmentSlot",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/AppointmentSlot"
          },
          "description": "Stores available appointment slots.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "appointmentSlotId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the appointment slot."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/appointments/{appointmentId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Appointment",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Appointment"
          },
          "description": "Stores booked appointments.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "appointmentId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the appointment."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/jobApplications/{jobApplicationId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "JobApplication",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/JobApplication"
          },
          "description": "Stores job applications.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "jobApplicationId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the job application."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/contactFormSubmissions/{contactFormSubmissionId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "ContactFormSubmission",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/ContactFormSubmission"
          },
          "description": "Stores contact form submissions.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "contactFormSubmissionId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the contact form submission."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/aiPrecisionRecovery/{aiPrecisionRecoveryId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "AiPrecisionRecovery",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/AiPrecisionRecovery"
          },
          "description": "Stores data for the AI Precision Recovery feature.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "aiPrecisionRecoveryId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the AI precision recovery data."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": "This Firestore structure is designed to support the Aries PhysioCare website and its connection to the Firebase Studio admin panel, adhering to the principles of Authorization Independence, Structural Segregation, Access Modeling, and Data Clarity.  The structure prioritizes read-only access for the website, with specific exceptions for appointment booking, job applications, and contact form submissions.\n\nAuthorization Independence is achieved by avoiding hierarchical authorization dependencies. Data related to services, therapists, locations, blogs, job openings, and FAQs can be read directly without needing to fetch parent document data.  User-generated content (appointments, job applications, contact form submissions) are stored in dedicated collections.\n\nStructural Segregation ensures that each collection has a homogenous security posture. Public data (services, therapists, locations, blogs, FAQs, JobOpenings, AiPrecisionRecovery) are stored separately from user-specific data (appointments, job applications, contact form submissions).\n\nAccess Modeling follows a path-based approach for user-generated content (appointments, job applications, contact form submissions).  This approach provides a straightforward way to manage access control and ensure that users can only access their own data.\n\nTo support the QAPs, the design leverages structural segregation.  Listing services, blogs, FAQs, etc., is secure because these collections only contain data intended to be publicly readable.  Write access to appointment, contact form and job application collections is governed by security rules validating the request data.\n\n"
  }
}
